{"content":[{"c":["SHALLUM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":[" 1. Son of Jabesh and Israel’s 16th king (752 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"). In a conspiracy against King Zechariah, Shallum murdered the monarch at Ibleam and declared himself ruler of Israel during the 39th year of King Uzziah’s (Azariah’s) reign in Judah (792–740 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"). However, in like manner, he was killed at the hands of Gadi after ruling for only one month (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.15.10-15","r":"2Kgs.15.10-15","rawR":"2Kgs.15.10-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.15.10-15","value":"2Kgs.15.10-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 15:10-15"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=ChronologyoftheBibleOldTestament_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"ChronologyoftheBibleOldTestament_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"ChronologyoftheBibleOldTestament_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Chronology of the Bible (Old Testament)"},"; ",{"href":"?item=IsraelHistoryof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"IsraelHistoryof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"IsraelHistoryof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Israel, History of"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 2. Son of Tikvah (alternately spelled Tokhath, see ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.34.22","r":"2Chr.34.22","rawR":"2Chr.34.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.34.22","value":"2Chr.34.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 34:22"},"), who was keeper of the wardrobe and the husband of Huldah the prophetess, living in Jerusalem during the days of King Josiah (640–609 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.22.14","r":"2Kgs.22.14","rawR":"2Kgs.22.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.22.14","value":"2Kgs.22.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 22:14"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 3. Sismai’s son and the father of Jekamiah from Judah’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.40-41","r":"1Chr.2.40-41","rawR":"1Chr.2.40-41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.40-41","value":"1Chr.2.40-41"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:40-41"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 4. Alternate name for Jehoahaz, the youngest of King Josiah’s four sons and later Judah’s 17th king, in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.3.15","r":"1Chr.3.15","rawR":"1Chr.3.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.3.15","value":"1Chr.3.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 3:15"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.22.11","r":"Jer.22.11","rawR":"Jer.22.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.22.11","value":"Jer.22.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jeremiah 22:11"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jehoahaz_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jehoahaz_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jehoahaz_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jehoahaz #2"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 5. Shaul’s son, Simeon’s grandson, and the father of Mibsam (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.25","r":"1Chr.4.25","rawR":"1Chr.4.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.25","value":"1Chr.4.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:25"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 6. Alternate name for Meshullam, Zadok’s son and Ezra’s forefather, in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.12-13","r":"1Chr.6.12-13","rawR":"1Chr.6.12-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.12-13","value":"1Chr.6.12-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 6:12-13"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.7.2","r":"Ezra.7.2","rawR":"Ezra.7.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.7.2","value":"Ezra.7.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezra 7:2"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Meshullam_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Meshullam_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Meshullam_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Meshullam #7"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 7. Alternate name for Shillem, the youngest of Naphtali’s four sons, in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.13","r":"1Chr.7.13","rawR":"1Chr.7.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.13","value":"1Chr.7.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 7:13"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=ShillemShillemite_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"ShillemShillemite_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"ShillemShillemite_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Shillem, Shillemite"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 8. Alternate name for Meshullam, Kore’s son and chief of the gatekeepers (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.17-19,31","r":"1Chr.9.17-19,31","rawR":"1Chr.9.17-19,31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.17-19,31","value":"1Chr.9.17-19,31"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:17-19, 31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.42","r":"Ezra.2.42","rawR":"Ezra.2.42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.42","value":"Ezra.2.42"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:42"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.45","r":"Neh.7.45","rawR":"Neh.7.45","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.45","value":"Neh.7.45"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:45"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Meshullam_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Meshullam_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Meshullam_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Meshullam #20"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 9. Ephraimite and the father of Jehizkiah (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.28.12","r":"2Chr.28.12","rawR":"2Chr.28.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.28.12","value":"2Chr.28.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 28:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["10. One of the Levitical gatekeepers who was encouraged by Ezra to divorce his foreign wife during the postexilic era (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.24","r":"Ezra.10.24","rawR":"Ezra.10.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.24","value":"Ezra.10.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:24"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["11. One of the descendants of Binnui who was encouraged by Ezra to divorce his foreign wife (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.42","r":"Ezra.10.42","rawR":"Ezra.10.42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.42","value":"Ezra.10.42"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:42"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["12. Hallohesh’s son and a ruler of Jerusalem who, along with his daughters, repaired the section of city wall next to the Tower of the Ovens (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.12","r":"Neh.3.12","rawR":"Neh.3.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.12","value":"Neh.3.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["13. Col-hozeh’s son and ruler of the Mizpah district, who rebuilt the Fountain Gate and the wall of the pool of Shelah of the king’s garden (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.15","r":"Neh.3.15","rawR":"Neh.3.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.15","value":"Neh.3.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["14. Uncle of Hanamel and Jeremiah, who sold to the latter his field at Anathoth during King Zedekiah’s reign (597–586 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.32.7","r":"Jer.32.7","rawR":"Jer.32.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.32.7","value":"Jer.32.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 32:7"},"). He is perhaps identifiable with #2 above."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["15. Maaseiah’s father. Maaseiah, keeper of the threshold, owned a chamber in the sanctuary during Jehoiakim’s reign (609–598 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.35.4","r":"Jer.35.4","rawR":"Jer.35.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.35.4","value":"Jer.35.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 35:4"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.52.24","r":"Jer.52.24","rawR":"Jer.52.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.52.24","value":"Jer.52.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"52:24"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Shallum","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 15:10-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.15.10-15","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.15.10-15","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.15.10-15"},{"anchorText":